---
// Core Components
---

<section class="components" id="components">
  <div class="container">
    <h2><span class="text-accent">##</span> Core Components</h2>
    <p class="text-dim">The engines that power the machine. Each one a self-contained module in the signal chain.</p>

    <!-- The Central Scrutinizer -->
    <div class="comp-card">
      <div class="comp-card__header">
        <span class="comp-card__icon">👁️</span>
        <h3>The Central Scrutinizer</h3>
        <span class="badge badge--initiated">● ACTIVE</span>
      </div>
      <div class="comp-card__body">
        <p>
          A tiny quantized local LLM (~1–3B params) running on a detached control-rate thread (~100 Hz) 
          that injects high-level, non-repetitive creativity into the audio stream. 
          Reads system telemetry and user directives, outputs patching commands parsed into CV values, 
          generative spoken-word narration, and non-diatonic chord substitutions.
        </p>
        <div class="comp-card__specs">
          <span class="comp-spec"><code>llama.cpp</code> locally</span>
          <span class="comp-spec">100 Hz control rate</span>
          <span class="comp-spec"><code>&lt; 50 ms</code> latency</span>
          <span class="comp-spec">TTS + vocoder output</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- SyBorg -->
    <div class="comp-card">
      <div class="comp-card__header">
        <span class="comp-card__icon">🎸</span>
        <h3>SyBorg — The Zappa Instant Composition Engine</h3>
        <span class="badge badge--initiated">● ACTIVE</span>
      </div>
      <div class="comp-card__body">
        <p>
          Real-time chromatic guitar solo generator using <strong>Xenochrony</strong> — metric-phasing 
          between a backing clock (120 BPM, 4/4) and a solo clock (94 BPM, 11/8). 
          Irrational tuplets, microtonal pitch bends, and hard-cut tape edits at runtime.
        </p>
        <div class="comp-card__specs">
          <code>--eyebrows 0.8</code>
          <code>--lets-be-serious 0.4</code>
          <code>--imaginary-notes 0.3</code>
          <code>--marital-aids 0.2</code>
          <code>--scrutinize</code>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- FTRT Architecture -->
    <div class="comp-card">
      <div class="comp-card__header">
        <span class="comp-card__icon">🕐</span>
        <h3>FTRT Look-Ahead Architecture</h3>
        <span class="badge badge--initiated">● ACTIVE</span>
      </div>
      <div class="comp-card__body">
        <p>
          Future-Time Real-Time architecture with a 4-bar look-ahead buffer (~4 sec at 120 BPM). 
          Separates <strong>composition</strong> (FTRT, ahead of playback), 
          <strong>control</strong> (The Central Scrutinizer at ~100 Hz), 
          and <strong>audio rendering</strong> (at sample rate, hard real-time).
        </p>
        <p class="text-dim">
          Predictive filter sweeps, anticipatory decrescendos, and xenochronic phase alignments — 
          all calculated 2.5 seconds before the audio hits the DAC.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Style Extraction -->
    <div class="comp-card">
      <div class="comp-card__header">
        <span class="comp-card__icon">🎯</span>
        <h3>Style Extraction Pipeline</h3>
        <span class="badge badge--initiated">● ACTIVE</span>
      </div>
      <div class="comp-card__body">
        <p>
          Quantifies a performer's expressive DNA into measurable probabilistic decision vectors — 
          groove profile, velocity distribution, ghost note density map, fill vocabulary — 
          stored as portable JSON style models that the Scrutinizer queries at runtime.
        </p>
        <div class="comp-card__specs">
          <span class="comp-spec">Velocity profiles</span>
          <span class="comp-spec">Ghost note maps</span>
          <span class="comp-spec">Groove quantization</span>
          <span class="comp-spec">Portable JSON models</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Logic Pro Bridge -->
    <div class="comp-card">
      <div class="comp-card__header">
        <span class="comp-card__icon">🔌</span>
        <h3>Logic Pro IAC Bridge</h3>
        <span class="badge badge--initiated">● ACTIVE</span>
      </div>
      <div class="comp-card__body">
        <p>
          MIDI-over-IAC integration that routes EA's Python composition engine directly into Logic Pro — 
          controlling Drum Kit Designer, Alchemy, and Native Instruments plugins. 
          Share a <code>.logicx</code> file instead of source code. Open and play.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .components {
    padding: 4rem 0;
  }

  .comp-card {
    background: var(--color-bg-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .comp-card:hover {
    border-color: var(--color-border-hover);
  }

  .comp-card__header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    background: var(--color-bg-elevated);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .comp-card__icon {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .comp-card__header h3 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--font-size-base);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .comp-card__body {
    padding: 1.25rem;
  }

  .comp-card__body p {
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .comp-card__specs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
  }

  .comp-card__specs code,
  .comp-spec {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    padding: 0.125em 0.5em;
    background: var(--color-bg-elevated);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    color: var(--color-text-dim);
  }
</style>
